.vscode
__pycache__
*.pyc
.claude

# Saved class-notes page dumps — reference material for writing a submission, never part
# of one. Matched at any depth and in every naming style past sessions have used:
#   s8-model-architectures/s8-class-notes/   s9-class-notes.html + s9-class-notes_files/
#   s3_class_notes.md (underscore)           s4_notes.html + s4_notes_files/ (no "class")
# The old rule was `*/*class-notes*`, which matched only the hyphenated form exactly one
# level down, so the S3 and S4 dumps were never covered — and being already tracked, they
# would not have been excluded even if it had. They were untracked with `git rm --cached`;
# the files are still on disk.
*class-notes*
*class_notes*
*_notes.html
*_notes_files/

# s6: shard payloads are derived data — tokenizing the committed corpus/ with the frozen
# tokenizer reproduces them byte-for-byte, and run_demo.py rebuilds them every run. The
# corpus snapshot, the generated submission_artifacts/ bundle and out/ page data ARE
# committed: corpus/ is the reproducibility anchor, and the assignment requires the
# generated manifests, ledgers and checkpoints to be part of the submission.
s06-dataset-creation/shards/
